@startuml sequence
title CHORAS Geometry Pipeline\nSequence — example scenario: wave-based profile, T-junctions stage

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

' --------------------------------------------------------------------------
' Scope of this diagram
' --------------------------------------------------------------------------
' This is ONE concrete scenario chosen because the T-junctions stage is the
' most interesting case (iterative repair with an injected detector).
' Lifelines are typed by their INTERFACE («interface» stereotype) so the
' protocol shown here applies to any RepairStep / Validator / Exporter the
' profile happens to plug in.
'
' For the GENERAL control flow (loop over all stages, fail-fast, FINAL
' detection, conditional export), see activity.puml — that diagram is the
' generic view; this one is the worked example.
' --------------------------------------------------------------------------

actor Client

box "Adapter layer (Flask + DB)" #FDF6E3
  participant ":HttpRoutes"                          as Routes
  participant "service\n:GeometryService"            as Service
  database    ":Repository"                          as DB
end box

box "app.geometry core" #EEF6FF
  participant "imp_reg\n:ImporterRegistry"           as ImpReg
  participant "importer\n«interface»\n:Importer"     as Imp
  participant ":Pipeline"                            as Pipe
  participant "pre\n«interface»\n:Validator[*]"      as PreV
  participant "stage_tj\n:Stage"                     as STJ
  participant "tj_repair\n«interface»\n:RepairStep"  as FixTJ
  participant "tj_detector\n«interface»\n:Validator" as VTJ
  participant "exporter\n«interface»\n:Exporter"     as Exp
end box

== upload ==
Client  -> Routes  : POST /upload (file.obj)
Routes  -> Service : handle_upload(file)
Service -> DB      : insert Model (status=PENDING)

== load ==
Service -> ImpReg  : get_for(".obj")
ImpReg  --> Service : :Importer
Service -> Imp     : load(path)
Imp     --> Service : :Geometry  (Mesh)

== orchestration ==
Service -> Pipe : run_pipeline(geom, profile, ctx)

Pipe -> PreV : detect(geom, ctx)
PreV --> Pipe : :ValidationSnapshot  (when=PRE)

== stage: fix T-junctions (iterative) ==
Pipe -> STJ   : run()
STJ  -> FixTJ : apply(geom, issues, ctx)

loop until detector returns empty OR max_iters reached
  FixTJ -> VTJ : detect(geom, ctx)
  VTJ   --> FixTJ : list<Issue>
  FixTJ -> FixTJ  : split affected edges
end

FixTJ --> STJ : (geom', :RepairResult)
STJ  -> VTJ  : detect(geom, ctx)
VTJ  --> STJ : list<Issue>
STJ  --> Pipe : :ValidationSnapshot  (when=POST_STAGE,\nstage_name="t_junctions")

note over Pipe
  Other stages declared by the profile (dedup, degenerate, orient,
  intersections, topology, ...) follow the same protocol as the
  T-junctions stage above and are omitted here for brevity.
  Their order and inclusion are profile-specific.
  See activity.puml for the generic loop over stages.
end note

== final detection ==
Pipe -> PreV : detect(geom, ctx)
PreV --> Pipe : :ValidationSnapshot  (when=FINAL)

== export ==
Pipe -> Exp : write(geom, output_path)
Exp  --> Pipe : output_path

Pipe --> Service : :PipelineResult\n(snapshots[], repairs, output_path)

== diffing & persistence ==
Service -> Service : diff_snapshots(prev, curr) per stage
Service -> DB      : update Model (status=READY)
Service -> DB      : insert Report (snapshots, diffs)
Service --> Routes : 200 OK + report id
Routes  --> Client : JSON

note right of Pipe
  Lifelines are typed by interface, so the interaction is valid
  for any concrete implementation chosen by the profile:
    :Importer   -> ObjImporter | DxfImporter | Rhino3dmImporter
    :Validator  -> TJunctions | NonPlanarFaces | ...
    :RepairStep -> FixTJunctionsIterative | TrimSegmentFace... | ...
    :Exporter   -> GmshGeoExporter | ObjExporter

  Each Issue carries:
    id (stable hash of kind+payload),
    when (PRE | POST_STAGE | FINAL),
    stage_name, severity, payload
  -> diff_snapshots(before, after) -> {fixed, introduced, remaining}
end note

@enduml
